-- Adapted from The Ultimate French Press Technique.
-- 30 g per 500 g is 60 g/L. The supported dose range is an app choice;
-- always leave room for grounds and headspace in your particular carafe.
-- Pour gets a practical 30-second allowance, not a prescribed Hoffmann timing.
-- Skim and serve advance manually. The guide uses the five-minute settling option.

= Prep =
Preheat the #French press{} with hot water, then discard it. Grind @coffee{30%g} medium and add it to the carafe. Have two spoons and a small bowl ready. Check that the displayed water amount fits your carafe with room for grounds and headspace; reduce the dose if needed. Use freshly boiled water. Start the timer with the first water. Confirm the skim and serve steps when you are done; they have no countdown.

= Add all the water =
Pour @water{500%g} onto the grounds over roughly ~{30%seconds}, wetting them all. This is one fill, not a separate bloom and several pours; the exact pour rate is not critical.

= Steep undisturbed =
Leave the coffee alone until ~until{4%minutes} on the brew clock. Do not stir or plunge yet.

= Break the crust and skim =
Gently stir through the crust with a spoon so the grounds sink. Use two spoons to scoop the remaining foam and floating grounds into the bowl. Continue when the crust is skimmed to begin settling.

= Let the grounds settle =
Leave the carafe completely still for ~{5%minutes} so the fine particles settle and the coffee cools. Hoffmann suggests five to eight minutes here; this guide uses five. For a longer rest, pause near the end of this step and resume when ready. Do not plunge or move the carafe.

= Serve gently, do not plunge =
Fit the lid and lower the mesh only until it touches the coffee's surface. Do not push it down through the coffee; use it as a strainer. Pour slowly and gently into your cup without disturbing the sediment, leaving the last muddy liquid behind. Confirm when you have finished serving.

= Finish =
Enjoy once the coffee is comfortable to drink. Leave the settled grounds and the last muddy liquid in the carafe; do not plunge them or pour them into the cup.
